  "appearance": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Horizontal Charge Gu and vertical crash Gu are rank three, and are the two main materials that, with primeval essence and supplementary materials, refine into Charging Crash Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          345
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "form-and-rank",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ],
    "visual_confidence": "text_described"
  },
  "abilities": {
    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Horizontal Charge Gu is similar to vertical crash Gu, except the charge runs sideways rather than straight ahead. Fang Yuan activates it and his body charges horizontally, smashing through stone pillars in training.",
        "chapters": [
          288
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Both Gu let the Gu Master exert force while moving, so the movement itself becomes an attack. They suit strength path Gu Masters especially well. Unlike jumping grass, whose leap comes from the worm, vertical crash Gu draws its break-through force from the Gu Master’s body and grows as that body grows stronger; Horizontal Charge Gu is its horizontal counterpart.",
        "chapters": [
          288
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_master",
          "path_strength",
          "fac_gu_masters"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Vertical crash Gu alone is stated at about fifty steps with a five-breath cooldown when used by itself.",
        "chapters": [
          290
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "When Fang Yuan alternates Horizontal Charge Gu and vertical crash Gu, he keeps a three-breath gap between them and accounts for about fifty steps per charge so one of the two movement Gu stays ready.",
        "chapters": [
          291
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "The two rank three Gu together cover only a hundred steps, before Charging Crash Gu raises the fused charge to two hundred and halves the delay between uses.",
        "chapters": [
          345
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "Against Li Hao he follows a vertical crash with Horizontal Charge Gu to close the remaining distance after the first charge falls short, forcing Li Hao to use position swap Gu. He keeps alternating the two Gu to dodge the mountain back toad and to press the fight.",
        "chapters": [
          290
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fang-yuans-early-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_li_hao",
          "gu_position_swap_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "He later uses Horizontal Charge Gu to evade Zhu Ba’s meatball charge, then turns with vertical crash Gu to keep attacking.",
        "chapters": [
          300
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fang-yuans-early-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_zhu_ba"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Against Ju Kai Bei he stops a vertical crash against a stone pillar, then fires Horizontal Charge Gu at close range to land a hit Ju Kai Bei fails to dodge.",
        "chapters": [
          318
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fang-yuans-early-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_ju_kai_bei"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "During the same match he keeps using both Gu to evade while healing with self-reliance Gu, even though dragon travel tiger steps Gu is faster than either charge Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          319
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fang-yuans-early-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_self_reliance_gu",
          "gu_dragon_travel_tiger_steps_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "On San Cha mountain he uses Horizontal Charge Gu then vertical crash Gu to leave Xue San Si’s diving attack range, then charges back into the crater with the same pair.",
        "chapters": [
          343
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "fang-yuans-early-use",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_san_cha_mountain",
          "char_xue_san_si"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
